{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01A4cN2g9kZm7H8chJuPnEnK","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tname: tone-guide\n3\tdescription: House style for release notes and changelog entries. Use when drafting or editing release notes.\n4\t---\n5\t\n6\t# tone-guide\n7\t\n8\tWhen you write or edit release notes:\n9\t\n10\t- Lead with what changed for the reader, not with what the team did.\n11\t- One idea per bullet. Keep bullets under 20 words.\n12\t- Use plain words: \"fixed\", \"added\", \"removed\". Avoid \"leveraged\" and \"utilized\".\n13\t- Name the user-visible effect of a fix, not the internal cause.\n14\t- If a change could surprise someone, say so first and say what to do about it.\n15\t- Never promise dates for future work.\n16\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01SVABXFQKsMJhwNe3FwxcZZ","session_id":"758a8ba6-cf79-465a-b631-7c006e421dcf","uuid":"761b2967-49e0-4f9e-aaf8-1d3dfe4a0990","timestamp":"2026-10-04T03:08:55.153Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Scan skills/tone-guide folder"}
